    {
      "id": "the-third-part-of-king-henry-the-sixth/sceneI_14.2/p@28049",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "YORK.\nAy, with my sword. What, think’st thou that we fear them?\nEdward and Richard, you shall stay with me;\nMy brother Montague shall post to London.\nLet noble Warwick, Cobham, and the rest,\nWhom we have left protectors of the King,\nWith powerful policy strengthen themselves,\nAnd trust not simple Henry nor his oaths.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
